      "problem": "Sketch the graph of $y=|x+1|+2$.",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x+1|+2$ has $h=-1$ and $k=2.$ Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $1$ unit *left* and $2$ units up.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/e80f640da0a2e6e6c1e14790f66b6a05747f6149dddc8a14fc48932bd5e696eb.png)",
